 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<token>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`: returns a page ordered by `id`.
+  Both query parameters are optional. `limit` defaults to 20; `cursor` is the
+  opaque `next_cursor` returned by the preceding page. `next_cursor` is `null`
+  on the last page. Invalid limits or cursors return HTTP-shaped status 400
+  with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
